@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #9ca3af

title One FindCare search end to end, target architecture: the gate is a dumb facade,\nthe UniversalNavigator drives the map, tools call tools, and prose is its own tool

participant "Gate\n(facade, transport only)" as Gate
participant "UniversalNavigator\n(SharedServices main)" as UN
participant "UtteranceManager\n(classify only)" as UM
participant "Prose tool\n(authors the sentence)" as Prose
database "Registry\n(the one live map)" as Reg
database "Repository\nsessions, ledger, params" as Repo
participant "facility_search\n(tool)" as FS
participant "Miner\nmine_facility_parameters" as Miner
participant "SpecialtyFilter\nNon-Individual" as Cat
database "Provider\ncollection" as Providers

[-> Gate : POST /  { session_token, head,\nparams(utterance, history) }  client_sessioned
activate Gate
note over Gate
  The gate knows only transport. It collects the token, the HTTP
  head, and the POST/GET parameters, each if present, and hands
  them to the navigator. It has no routes of its own; one generic
  gate module serves every container.
end note

Gate -> UN : navigate(session_token, head, params)
activate UN
UN -> Reg : the live map for this env\n(routes, may_call, required inputs)
Reg --> UN : routes + dependencies
note left of UN
  The navigator holds no data. The map is the registry,
  parameters ride the passed document, the session and the
  render ledger are repository rows. It is the only node
  that accepts external traffic.
end note
UN -> Repo : verify session_token, advance nonce,\nload parameters in force
Repo --> UN : session ok, in-force parameters

UN -> UM : classify(utterance, history)
activate UM
UM --> UN : dispatch set { facility_search }
deactivate UM
note right of UM
  One model call: the cached preamble plus every tool's registry
  fragment in, routes out. It knows no parameters and never waits
  on a tool - it returns the set; parallelism is the point.
end note

UN -> Repo : record the render-ledger expectation
UN -> FS : dispatch { utterance, history, in-force params }
activate FS
FS -> Miner : mine(utterance, history)
activate Miner
Miner --> FS : geography, facilityType, facilityName
deactivate Miner
alt a kind of place was named
  FS -> Cat : find_specialties(facilityType, Non-Individual)
  activate Cat
  Cat --> FS : offered kinds + codes
  deactivate Cat
end
FS -> Providers : state of the ZIP, when no state was said
Providers --> FS : derived state
note over FS, Cat
  Tools call tools directly along the non-circular may_call map,
  with recursion guards. A tool in the middle re-raises and never
  swallows; every throw ends in a navigator, which catches,
  classifies, logs with timings, and answers.
end note
FS --> UN : completion callback { mined document }\ninternal_callback, proof our_signature
deactivate FS
UN -> Repo : close the ledger entry, then serial deterministic\nmerge into parameter state (a conflict is an exception)
UN -> UN : completeness test - the passed document\nagainst the registry's required inputs

alt required inputs all in force
  UN -> FS : dispatch { search: codes, place }
  activate FS
  FS -> Providers : search_providers(entity_type = "2", codes, place)
  Providers --> FS : rows + total
  FS --> UN : completion callback { rows }\ninternal_callback, proof our_signature
  deactivate FS
  UN -> Repo : close the ledger entry, serial merge the rows
else a required input is unmet
  UN -> Prose : author refinement { unmet, in force, utterance }
  activate Prose
  Prose --> UN : the user-facing sentence
  deactivate Prose
  note right of Prose
    User-facing prose is its own tool. The navigator dispatches it
    with the facts; it returns one sentence. No tool authors its
    own chat strings; making a parameter required is an edit to the
    registry and a deploy, not a line of code.
  end note
end

UN --> Gate : the merged answer, sequenced
deactivate UN
[<-- Gate : the one stream the gate writes
deactivate Gate

@enduml
